# tools/d/distance_witness.rish -- the chamfer distance transform proves itself on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- the distance transform the label rung named. Where image/label.rye partitions a mask into
# its connected pieces (a GLOBAL topology), this rung reads a mask's METRIC structure: for each foreground pixel it measures the
# chamfer distance to the nearest background pixel, the field whose local maxima trace a shape's spine -- exactly what the
# skeleton and zhang_suen rungs thin a shape down toward. The algorithm is the classic chamfer 3-4 transform (Borgefors, 1986):
# a forward raster pass and a backward reverse-raster pass, each relaxing four neighbors, weighting an orthogonal step 3 and a
# diagonal step 4 -- an integer approximation of the Euclidean distance with no floating point and no square root.
#
# The crux this witness proves on metal: a solid 3x3 block reads 3 around its ring and 6 at its center (one and two orthogonal
# steps from the edge); a pixel touching a lone background hole only at its CORNER reads 4 not 3 (the diagonal weight); the same
# hole at the BOTTOM-RIGHT is reached only on the backward pass (the second pass's reason to exist); foreground is read by
# red >= 128 through branch.is_on (one binary door) so a faint mark still measures; an all-background mask is 0 with max_distance
# 0; colorize renders the field to a real image that round-trips through the open QOI codec byte-for-byte; an empty source refuses
# by name; the same mask measures deterministically. No network, no key, no funds -- the depth a surface reads the day it asks how
# thick a mark is, on our own open geometry.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/d/distance_witness.rish

say "distance: Language EN -- Season G chamfer distance transform; measure every foreground pixel of a mask to the nearest background pixel."
say "distance: Style Radiant -- compose not braid: this rung owns only the chamfer weights, the two-pass sweep, and the render ramp; branch.is_on decides the binary meaning of a pixel, qoi owns the buffers, color.mix blends the ramp."
say "distance: Lens TAME -- the distance buffer is bounded by the pixel count and a chamfer distance never exceeds 4 * max dimension, so dist_far sits far above any real distance and below maxInt(u32); the source is refused by name up front so a refusal allocates nothing; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/distance"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/distance.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "distance: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "distance: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "distance: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-distance" else "distance: selftest did not print the GREEN line"

say "distance: GREEN -- a 3x3 block reads 3 around its ring and 6 at its center, a corner-adjacent pixel reads 4 (the diagonal weight), a bottom-right hole is reached only on the backward pass, colorize round-trips through the open QOI codec, on metal."
